    "title": "Donations needed to increase blood supply",
    "text": "Registration is open for a blood drive from 11:30 a.m. to 6:30 p.m. Tuesday, Jan. 27, at the recreation center, 41 Conanicus Ave.\nThe drive, administered by the Rhode Island Blood Center, is being co-sponsored by the local VFW and American Legion posts in honor of James McLoughlin, a World War II veteran who donated more than 400 times before his death in 2015.\nRegister through RIBC.org/drives by using code 0894.\nDonors must be 17 years old and weigh at least 110 pounds; 16-year-olds can donate blood with written consent from a parent and if they weigh more than 130 pounds.",
